WEBVTT

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:12.040
What's this big lake?

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:15.150
There wasn't one in the 
Story Zone you're from, huh, Ex?

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:17.020
It's called the sea.

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:17.830
The sea?

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:20.520
It's much bigger than any lake!

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.140
It's also the setting for many stories—

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:27.680
Come on, you two! What are you doing?

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:29.110
It's been ages since we hit the beach!

00:00:29.110 --> 00:00:30.210
Let's take a dip!

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:31.670
Don't be stupid!

00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:32.950
Here I come!

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:40.300
What's with this water? It's salty!

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:42.350
That's the taste of the sea!

00:00:43.310 --> 00:00:45.180
Take this!

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:47.940
Are they children?

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:50.840
So be it.

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:53.070
Shane, at least the two of us can...

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:57.690
Boss, do you prefer bikinis or one-pieces?

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.630
Where did you get those?

00:00:59.630 --> 00:01:00.180
Huh?

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:01.610
Don't "huh" me!

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:04.460
Who's that?

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:07.460
He was floating in the water 
with some ship wreckage.

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:10.340
Hey, are you okay?

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:12.520
My name is Silver.

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:15.220
I've been searching for this place... 
Treasure Island.

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:18.010
Treasure Island?!

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:52.020
Treasure Island, a Place of Dreams and Adventure

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:57.290
Thanks again.

00:02:57.290 --> 00:03:00.680
I'm John Silver. Just a poor hired cook.

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:03.030
So, is it true?

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:04.070
Yeah.

00:03:04.070 --> 00:03:08.330
Our ship was on a course 
for Treasure Island.

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:10.370
But as soon as we saw it on the horizon,

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:13.170
monsters leapt out of the sea...

00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:15.020
Were there any other survivors?

00:03:16.490 --> 00:03:18.300
I'm probably the only one.

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:22.480
The ship went up in flames,
 and when everybody jumped ship...

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:23.890
there were more monsters.

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:28.390
My Book of Fate didn't say 
anything about this.

00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:30.600
What does it say?

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:31.640
Curious?

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:39.030
Once upon a time, there was a 
terrifying pirate named Flint.

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:45.400
He was the terror of the high seas, 
stealing all the treasure he could find.

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:50.650
And when his time drew near, 
he hid his booty away on a certain island.

00:03:50.650 --> 00:03:52.320
Soon after, he died.

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:57.920
For many years, no one 
could find Flint's treasure.

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:04.590
But by chance, a boy at an inn 
obtained a map to where it was hidden.

00:04:05.210 --> 00:04:09.930
And my Book of Fate said 
I was going to help him.

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:11.390
I see...

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:15.100
That must be the plot of this Story Zone—
the story of Treasure Island.

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:18.480
Did the boy with the map 
go down with the ship?

00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:19.480
Yeah.

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:26.200
You should still be resting!

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:28.330
No can do.

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:30.200
I've got a dream.

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:31.330
A dream?

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:32.580
Yeah.

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:34.670
I want to be a pirate like Flint...

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:38.750
No, even better!

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:40.820
But your Book of Fate...

00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:43.450
It doesn't matter.

00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:46.510
Fish were meant for the sea.
Birds were meant for the sky.

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:49.760
And men were meant for adventure.

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:51.220
Know what I mean?

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:56.310
I can't bear to watch, Silver.

00:04:56.310 --> 00:04:58.400
But I get where you're coming from.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:00.330
So I have an offer...

00:05:00.330 --> 00:05:01.190
An offer?

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:03.320
Let me, the great Tao, help you!

00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:04.650
H-Hang on!

00:05:04.910 --> 00:05:08.200
Of course, the rest of the Tao 
family will pitch in, too!

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:11.620
"The rest of the Tao family"?

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:14.830
That's definitely us, right?

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:18.290
Hold on just a minute! I never said 
you could call us the Tao family!

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:20.520
And why do we have 
to help find the treasure—

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:22.340
Let's go, Silver!

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:25.290
A manly adventure awaits!

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:29.260
Listen to me!

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:32.660
Stop laughing!

00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:37.440
Somehow it feels like 
I'm getting used to this.

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:39.970
That's a good sign, new kid.

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:47.280
Sorry, Brother Tao has a weakness for 
words like "dreams" and "adventure."

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:52.060
I don't really care about that stuff, 
but maybe this is for the best.

00:05:53.090 --> 00:05:56.540
Silver came here from a distant port.

00:05:56.540 --> 00:06:01.670
But rather than arriving at port 
in this Story Zone, we were here.

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:03.460
Which means...

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:06.190
The Chaos Teller is on this island?

00:06:07.350 --> 00:06:09.060
You're sure this is the way?

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:12.470
Look.

00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:15.490
This is the map Flint left behind.

00:06:15.490 --> 00:06:19.030
If you had something like that, 
you should've said so!

00:06:19.030 --> 00:06:20.900
It's tough to walk with all these rocks.

00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:25.940
But I've got no idea what all 
these symbols on it mean.

00:06:26.260 --> 00:06:29.570
Flint was an extremely wary man.

00:06:29.930 --> 00:06:33.330
One of them is probably a trap.

00:06:33.520 --> 00:06:34.990
What's this?

00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:36.620
Where are we now?

00:06:37.050 --> 00:06:38.250
Here.

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:39.720
Eyes open, everybody!

00:06:39.720 --> 00:06:41.050
Don't touch anything weird—

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:44.340
Hey!

00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:51.930
I have a bad feeling...

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:54.860
Strange. So do I.

00:06:58.580 --> 00:07:00.440
What were you thinking, missy?!

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:02.900
If I wasn't supposed to do that,
 you should've told me!

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:04.270
It's almost on top of us, Tao!

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:09.110
M-Me, too!

00:07:13.230 --> 00:07:15.350
H-How do I dodge it?

00:07:15.350 --> 00:07:16.580
Go right!

00:07:17.050 --> 00:07:18.000
Got it!

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:19.370
That's left!

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:25.750
Reina!

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:31.260
Boss...

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:32.720
Are you all right?

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:38.470
Y-Yeah, I'm just f-f-fine...

00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:46.320
Do you understand now?
Don't touch anything suspicious!

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:47.820
All right already!

00:07:49.750 --> 00:07:53.780
That mess threw us way off track.

00:07:53.780 --> 00:07:55.530
Where's the treasure?

00:07:56.040 --> 00:07:57.330
This inlet to the north.

00:07:57.570 --> 00:08:00.540
Most of the island's 
perimeter is steep cliffs.

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:02.330
You can't get a ship near 'em.

00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:06.040
The southern beach I washed up on
 is the only way in and out.

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:10.300
So if you want the treasure, 
you have to traverse the island?

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:13.050
Yeah. He could set up
all the traps he wanted.

00:08:17.860 --> 00:08:19.010
This is...

00:08:19.010 --> 00:08:21.020
Pretty deep.

00:08:21.870 --> 00:08:22.730
Oh?

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:24.980
A bridge!

00:08:25.760 --> 00:08:26.630
Wait.

00:08:27.330 --> 00:08:28.940
We're about here right now.

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:31.650
First an X, and now an O?

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:34.400
That may be a clever trap in itself.

00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:35.490
You're right.

00:08:35.490 --> 00:08:37.490
It's safer just to go around...

00:08:40.740 --> 00:08:42.660
Hey, missy! The hell are you doing?!

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:43.830
Don't try to cross that!

00:08:44.170 --> 00:08:46.000
I was just checking it out!

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:52.920
Thanks, Shane.

00:08:53.170 --> 00:08:54.550
Did you call me?

00:09:02.850 --> 00:09:05.190
Must be a treasure hunter who didn't make it.

00:09:05.190 --> 00:09:06.210
Are you all right?

00:09:06.210 --> 00:09:08.770
O-Of course!

00:09:15.060 --> 00:09:20.740
No pulling ropes, no crossing bridges,
 and no hugging skeletons!

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:22.290
I did <i>not</i> hug it!

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:27.040
But the way he put all these traps up...

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:29.380
That's just who Flint was.

00:09:29.380 --> 00:09:33.170
Terrifyingly smart, cold, and cruel.

00:09:33.170 --> 00:09:35.350
A great pirate feared by all.

00:09:35.350 --> 00:09:37.720
And that's what you wanna be?

00:09:37.980 --> 00:09:39.390
Don't you get it?

00:09:39.390 --> 00:09:42.060
The scarier a guy is,
 the more attractive he is.

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:45.490
Sounds like you want to be the bad guy.

00:09:45.490 --> 00:09:46.600
No way...

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:48.940
Nobody sets out to be a bad guy.

00:09:50.960 --> 00:09:51.980
What's wrong?

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:54.900
I thought I saw movement over there.

00:09:58.090 --> 00:09:59.570
Is it a villain?

00:10:12.980 --> 00:10:15.130
So there is a Chaos Teller on the island...

00:10:18.370 --> 00:10:19.690
That scared me.

00:10:21.960 --> 00:10:23.340
A lake, huh?

00:10:25.910 --> 00:10:28.690
Oh? Are they edible?

00:10:28.690 --> 00:10:30.310
Missy...

00:10:30.310 --> 00:10:31.440
I know!

00:10:34.250 --> 00:10:35.900
We're getting close to the treasure.

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:40.280
We're here right now.

00:10:40.280 --> 00:10:43.120
And our destination is this inlet here.

00:10:44.940 --> 00:10:47.080
Looks fine to me!

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:49.830
There's something written by the lake,

00:10:49.830 --> 00:10:50.870
but it's faded.

00:10:51.080 --> 00:10:53.100
Some kind of symbol?

00:10:55.250 --> 00:10:56.380
Hey, missy!

00:10:57.170 --> 00:10:58.260
I-I'm not going to eat it!

00:10:58.260 --> 00:11:00.430
I was just wondering
 what kind of fruit it was!

00:11:07.130 --> 00:11:07.880
Crap!

00:11:15.540 --> 00:11:17.650
Looks like we've got company.

00:11:17.650 --> 00:11:18.530
Shane?

00:11:18.530 --> 00:11:21.020
I'll go scout it out.

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:28.620
Wow. I didn't know Shane 
could move like that.

00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:30.460
U-Um, Ex...

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:31.960
Thank you.

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:34.560
Let's go after them, too.

00:11:49.110 --> 00:11:50.350
Maybe they won't find me here...

00:11:50.350 --> 00:11:52.520
Maybe they will.

00:11:52.870 --> 00:11:57.480
H-How can a girl run up 
a steep cliff like that?!

00:11:57.480 --> 00:12:00.720
I grew up on a similar deserted island.

00:12:00.720 --> 00:12:03.110
Anyway, why did you run?

00:12:03.110 --> 00:12:04.650
B-Because...

00:12:04.650 --> 00:12:06.620
You were with Silver.

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:08.740
You know him?

00:12:08.740 --> 00:12:10.450
We were on the same ship.

00:12:10.450 --> 00:12:12.290
Then he's on your side.

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:14.420
He is not!

00:12:15.650 --> 00:12:16.420
This way?

00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:18.430
Yeah, I see footprints.

00:12:19.090 --> 00:12:20.300
Brother Tao!

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:22.300
Is that the person?

00:12:22.510 --> 00:12:24.510
Huh? It's a kid.

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:28.560
He was on the same ship with 
Mr. Dreams and Adventure, he says.

00:12:28.950 --> 00:12:32.850
Are you the boy from the inn 
that Silver mentioned?

00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:34.100
Yeah, that's me...

00:12:34.310 --> 00:12:36.520
I'm glad you're safe.

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:38.440
Silver's gonna be thrilled.

00:12:38.440 --> 00:12:40.300
Hey, Silver!

00:12:40.780 --> 00:12:42.990
No! We need to run!

00:12:43.960 --> 00:12:45.820
He's not our friend!

00:12:45.820 --> 00:12:46.920
He worked for Flint...

00:12:49.350 --> 00:12:50.170
What's going on?

00:12:50.630 --> 00:12:51.410
Crap!

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:52.880
The entrance!

00:12:54.530 --> 00:12:56.000
Sorry, Tao.

00:12:56.260 --> 00:12:57.060
What?

00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:03.670
I even pretended to be drowning
 in order to get you on my side.

00:13:03.670 --> 00:13:06.300
But now that you've met Jim, it's all over.

00:13:06.460 --> 00:13:09.130
I'm afraid you'll just
 have to rest in there...

00:13:09.130 --> 00:13:10.180
Forever!

00:13:10.180 --> 00:13:12.590
Hey, Silver! Silver!

00:13:15.070 --> 00:13:17.430
It really is too bad, Tao...

00:13:22.820 --> 00:13:28.090
John Silver was originally 
a helmsman on Flint's ship.

00:13:28.090 --> 00:13:29.570
A pirate.

00:13:29.850 --> 00:13:32.700
He came aboard our ship as a cook

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:35.540
in order to steal the treasure for himself.

00:13:35.730 --> 00:13:39.380
So did you see the monster 
that attacked your ship?

00:13:39.520 --> 00:13:42.800
See it?! Silver was the monster!

00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:44.160
Then...

00:13:44.160 --> 00:13:47.550
Yes, John Silver is the Chaos Teller.

00:13:47.810 --> 00:13:51.740
I survived by jumping into the 
water at the last second, but...

00:13:54.280 --> 00:13:55.680
You did great.

00:13:58.280 --> 00:14:04.230
If we didn't have blank books, maybe he 
would've turned us into villains by now.

00:14:04.230 --> 00:14:06.950
I'm going to make him pay.

00:14:07.340 --> 00:14:08.150
Hey, Shane!

00:14:08.480 --> 00:14:09.780
This, right?

00:14:09.780 --> 00:14:11.320
Where'd you get that?!

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:16.540
Smokeless gunpowder, a more 
advanced form of black powder!

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:19.770
I picked it up in a previous Story Zone!

00:14:20.760 --> 00:14:23.500
And it's finally time to use it!

00:14:25.990 --> 00:14:28.630
Now, everyone, stand back.

00:14:32.480 --> 00:14:33.370
What?

00:14:33.370 --> 00:14:35.820
The fuse was too short.

00:14:41.120 --> 00:14:44.840
Wow! What a wonderful explosion!

00:14:44.840 --> 00:14:45.900
That was great!

00:14:46.200 --> 00:14:47.820
I thought I was dead...

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:50.530
Hey, kiddo, you know where 
the treasure is, right?

00:14:50.530 --> 00:14:54.370
Y-Yeah... Silver took my map, though.

00:14:54.550 --> 00:14:55.240
Okay!

00:14:55.240 --> 00:14:59.540
I ain't leaving until I sock him a good one!

00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:01.320
Let's go, guys!

00:15:10.710 --> 00:15:12.090
This ship...

00:15:12.090 --> 00:15:12.800
You know it?

00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:15.560
It appears to be a type of galleon,

00:15:15.690 --> 00:15:19.100
but it's been modified here and there
and covered with cannons!

00:15:19.100 --> 00:15:22.600
It's even got a battle ram!

00:15:22.600 --> 00:15:25.250
It's practically a warship!

00:15:25.950 --> 00:15:26.610
I see...

00:15:26.610 --> 00:15:28.900
This must be Flint's ship!

00:15:28.900 --> 00:15:30.740
The treasure is inside!

00:15:30.940 --> 00:15:32.570
Hey, kiddo!

00:15:37.390 --> 00:15:38.580
Look at this!

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:41.410
The treasure was real after all!

00:15:42.620 --> 00:15:44.500
Just look at all this gold!

00:15:44.500 --> 00:15:46.250
It's so shiny!

00:15:46.250 --> 00:15:47.380
Come on, everybody!

00:15:50.020 --> 00:15:50.530
Jim!

00:15:55.230 --> 00:15:56.300
Why...

00:15:56.300 --> 00:15:58.800
He fell for it.

00:16:01.670 --> 00:16:02.860
Silver!

00:16:06.650 --> 00:16:08.530
What the hell did you do?!

00:16:08.660 --> 00:16:11.240
I just cast a little spell.

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:15.420
A trap that makes anyone who touches 
the treasure share my dream.

00:16:15.420 --> 00:16:16.450
Your dream?

00:16:16.720 --> 00:16:20.450
To be a greater pirate than Flint!

00:16:21.920 --> 00:16:26.670
So from now on, 
he's one of Silver's crew.

00:16:26.870 --> 00:16:28.340
You bastard!

00:16:28.490 --> 00:16:32.500
For some reason, it seems 
that won't work on you, though.

00:16:33.960 --> 00:16:37.980
So I'll be getting rid of you here
 to keep you from causing any trouble!

00:16:42.130 --> 00:16:45.270
I'm gonna make you pay!

00:16:46.040 --> 00:16:47.440
Don't make me laugh.

00:16:47.440 --> 00:16:52.070
Silver's crew rules the seven seas.
Don't think you can beat us!

00:17:02.470 --> 00:17:03.620
Everybody ready?

00:17:03.620 --> 00:17:07.250
This'll be the Tao family's biggest fight yet!

00:17:08.650 --> 00:17:09.880
Connect!

00:17:12.540 --> 00:17:16.000
Look! I got a new swimsuit! 
Great, isn't it?

00:17:26.030 --> 00:17:27.810
What's with these outfits?

00:17:27.810 --> 00:17:28.690
Swimsuits?

00:17:28.690 --> 00:17:30.360
They look easy to move in!

00:17:30.360 --> 00:17:32.100
Is that the issue?

00:17:32.100 --> 00:17:34.610
It doesn't matter whether 
we're in swimsuits or buck naked!

00:17:34.610 --> 00:17:36.470
Let's do this, everyone!

00:17:37.250 --> 00:17:39.410
Get 'em, men!

00:17:40.530 --> 00:17:42.290
Here I go!

00:17:42.500 --> 00:17:44.540
Vacation Spear!

00:17:45.070 --> 00:17:48.290
Want to go in the water with me?

00:17:48.520 --> 00:17:51.170
Summer Night Aureole!

00:17:52.640 --> 00:17:53.920
I can help, too!

00:17:54.800 --> 00:17:57.340
Summer Wolf Buster!

00:18:00.190 --> 00:18:01.970
You're not bad.

00:18:01.970 --> 00:18:04.200
But it wouldn't be fun any other way.

00:18:04.200 --> 00:18:08.110
You think I'd let you sit 
this one out, John Silver?

00:18:08.930 --> 00:18:11.370
I thought you'd come, Tao!

00:18:13.080 --> 00:18:16.740
Fool! I'm the captain of Silver's crew!

00:18:16.740 --> 00:18:18.420
That won't work on me!

00:18:21.400 --> 00:18:24.370
Was your dream to become a monster?

00:18:24.520 --> 00:18:27.540
You'd never understand...

00:18:30.930 --> 00:18:36.970
...how it feels to have your Book of Fate 
tell you your dream will never come true!

00:18:36.970 --> 00:18:37.970
Your dream?

00:18:38.130 --> 00:18:39.090
That's right!

00:18:39.090 --> 00:18:41.470
No matter what I do,
 I'll never get my treasure!

00:18:41.470 --> 00:18:43.070
I'll never be like Flint!

00:18:43.070 --> 00:18:45.850
I'll only ever be a fugitive on the run!

00:18:46.020 --> 00:18:49.270
Do you know how it feels to have 
that decided before you're even born?!

00:18:51.400 --> 00:18:54.570
Even so, what you're doing is wrong!

00:18:55.380 --> 00:18:57.180
I'm fine with that.

00:18:57.180 --> 00:18:58.400
If I don't do this,

00:18:59.090 --> 00:19:02.870
I'll never escape these fetters of fate!

00:19:13.560 --> 00:19:15.750
We're done here!

00:19:16.680 --> 00:19:18.260
Let's go save Tao!

00:19:18.470 --> 00:19:19.880
You're tough.

00:19:26.340 --> 00:19:28.270
The cannons are still working?

00:19:31.760 --> 00:19:33.010
Ouch!

00:19:33.010 --> 00:19:34.450
There's sand in my eyes!

00:19:34.450 --> 00:19:35.980
My swimsuit's coming off!

00:19:35.980 --> 00:19:40.070
Pirates always keep an ace up their sleeve!

00:19:41.610 --> 00:19:43.580
Fire, fire, and fire some more!

00:19:43.580 --> 00:19:47.120
And then let their bodies feed my dreams!

00:19:47.120 --> 00:19:48.840
Y-You bastard...

00:19:51.760 --> 00:19:55.670
I'll wake you up from this twisted dream.

00:19:55.980 --> 00:19:57.750
Sunshine Rain!

00:20:03.380 --> 00:20:06.140
What is this? This light?

00:20:11.390 --> 00:20:13.860
Captain... Flint?

00:20:17.710 --> 00:20:20.380
Now there's something I didn't want to see...

00:20:27.100 --> 00:20:31.910
I guess my dream never will come true, huh?

00:20:33.150 --> 00:20:33.800
Damn.

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:38.150
What a waste of a life...

00:20:43.020 --> 00:20:44.380
We're done here.

00:20:44.380 --> 00:20:47.050
If we'd been any later, 
things might've been bad.

00:20:47.340 --> 00:20:48.600
Please, missy.

00:20:48.600 --> 00:20:51.890
It's rare for you to ask me for anything...

00:20:51.890 --> 00:20:52.770
But I understand.

00:20:54.150 --> 00:20:55.430
I'm on it.

00:20:59.610 --> 00:21:02.540
Teller of tales, 
drowned in a maelstrom of chaos...

00:21:03.060 --> 00:21:07.320
By my words, I now begin the tuning...

00:21:17.320 --> 00:21:20.000
Jim and his friends finished 
loading the treasure.

00:21:20.220 --> 00:21:20.870
Yeah.

00:21:20.870 --> 00:21:23.720
The Treasure Island Story Zone 
is back to normal.

00:21:23.720 --> 00:21:24.800
I hate to say it,

00:21:24.800 --> 00:21:26.380
but this is goodbye to the sea.

00:21:26.380 --> 00:21:27.890
Where's Tao, by the way?

00:21:27.890 --> 00:21:31.640
Oh, he said he forgot something and ran off.

00:21:31.640 --> 00:21:34.020
I think he'll be back soon.

00:21:34.020 --> 00:21:36.230
I swear... What is he doing?

00:21:36.230 --> 00:21:39.980
Something he felt he had to 
as a man, I'm sure.

00:21:40.210 --> 00:21:41.570
Silver escaped!

00:21:41.570 --> 00:21:43.100
Where'd he go?!

00:21:43.550 --> 00:21:44.990
I'm better than all of you!

00:21:45.320 --> 00:21:46.610
No matter where I go

00:21:46.610 --> 00:21:48.660
or what I get into...

00:21:48.660 --> 00:21:51.630
if I want to, I can start over.

00:21:53.720 --> 00:21:55.750
Right, Flint?

00:22:00.330 --> 00:22:03.450
Jeez... You never learn.

00:22:03.450 --> 00:22:05.920
But there's nothing wrong with that.

00:23:42.940 --> 00:23:44.690
I have a report.

00:23:44.690 --> 00:23:49.690
The Priestess of Tuning has overwritten 
the Chaos Teller on Treasure Island.

00:23:49.890 --> 00:23:51.240
I see.

00:23:51.240 --> 00:23:52.740
What shall we do?

00:23:52.740 --> 00:23:54.230
There's another...

00:23:54.820 --> 00:23:58.080
She has someone with
 a wild crest with her now.

00:23:58.080 --> 00:24:00.750
I'm surprised you knew.

00:24:01.080 --> 00:24:04.350
I can't wait to meet them myself!
